{"step_index":10508,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-26T13:18:41Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-26T13:18:41Z\nCompleted At: 2026-09-26T13:18:43Z\nThe search for \"site:antigravity.google \"directory structure\" OR \"folder structure\" OR \"plugins\"\" returned the following summary:\nIn Google Antigravity, plugins are structured as directories containing a required `plugin.json` manifest file and optional subdirectories for various components[1][2][3]. When installed, these are typically staged in your home directory under `~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/plugins/<plugin_name>/`[3].\n\n### Plugin Directory Structure\nA typical plugin directory is organized as follows[2][3]:\n\n*   `plugin.json`: **Required**. The manifest file identifying the directory as a plugin and defining its metadata[2][3].\n*   `mcp_config.json`: Optional. Definitions for Model Context Protocol (MCP) servers[2][3].\n*   `hooks.json`: Optional. Definitions for event hooks[2][3].\n*   `skills/`: Optional. Subdirectories containing `SKILL.md` files for agent instructions[2][3].\n*   `agents/`: Optional. Markdown files defining custom subagent templates[4][2][3].\n*   `rules/`: Optional. Markdown files defining behavioral constraints or style guidelines[4][2][3].\n\n### Related Configuration Structures\n\n#### Sidecars\nSidecars are background processes managed by Antigravity[5]. They are discovered via `sidecar.json` files and can be located in[5]:\n*   **Global:** `~/.gemini/config/sidecars/`\n*   **Plugin-based:** `~/.gemini/config/plugins/<pluginName>/sidecars/`\n\nExample sidecar directory structure[5]:\n```text\n~/.gemini/config/sidecars/\n├── sidecar1/\n│   ├── sidecar.json\n│   └── script.py\n└── sidecar2/\n    └── sidecar.json\n```\n\n#### Skills\nWhile skills can be part of plugins, they can also be managed globally or per-workspace[6]. The standard directory is `.agents/skills/`[6]. Each skill is a folder containing a `SKILL.md` file[6][7]:\n```text\n.agents/skills/\n└── my-skill/\n    ├── SKILL.md      # Required instructions\n    ├── scripts/      # Optional helper scripts\n    └── examples/     # Optional reference implementations\n```\n\nSources:\n[1] [antigravity.google](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH_38uYx2BJdcCsRGv1Qge92G1cxriKGvz3w8bm4-Ud0CBDBetSk3X4AIxKTKNDHc7jJExkNspSdhMEmxfLUUFRBd5egsQ_GE7fS4hcyB52iOm4Ytv0_n4j1jn6FglI)\n[2] [antigravity.google](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH_38uYx2BJdcCsRGv1Qge92G1cxriKGvz3w8bm4-Ud0CBDBetSk3X4AIxKTKNDHc7jJExkNspSdhMEmxfLUUFRBd5egsQ_GE7fS4hcyB52iOm4Ytv0_n4j1jn6FglI)\n[3] [antigravity.google](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGxz1WJVyi8-B4jgrvf9EWSNUXCBW0YlJqKxRiUIzwhjoyA_uJhYXQRToDMxwZl6Sd6UV4ZTDmRhj50kE5vfLB8cfuoDVU1ulrhm003pj7p3E_EzmWXrclxWiVW1nFue13q-NQ=)\n[4] [antigravity.google](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQH_38uYx2BJdcCsRGv1Qge92G1cxriKGvz3w8bm4-Ud0CBDBetSk3X4AIxKTKNDHc7jJExkNspSdhMEmxfLUUFRBd5egsQ_GE7fS4hcyB52iOm4Ytv0_n4j1jn6FglI)\n[5] [antigravity.google](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGJNi4_QmwfyT1lW6nD9_hE9Ayn0orA0SaPEnnbJt7JjIBLYWZcniNoXF26_0DUF-ctvg23OESXC4ZazEG6tZcrAJnW7XHovZXhAifpa-r9KgVOvgpPiSgXdrkKJSJrBg==)\n[6] [antigravity.google](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlox4G64zm77cB82Oz-_3Xi4EZQDCuuC8CDib1txYjE0Qjc8Is_6Oy1v528-Q5h_VdAb0RgSVXWG5TPAMS0nFT5xBLSverrmmlLN-dAYWU0q_LG5p6aumLWylDoihmRCpH)\n[7] [antigravity.google](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGlox4G64zm77cB82Oz-_3Xi4EZQDCuuC8CDib1txYjE0Qjc8Is_6Oy1v528-Q5h_VdAb0RgSVXWG5TPAMS0nFT5xBLSverrmmlLN-dAYWU0q_LG5p6aumLWylDoihmRCpH)"}
{"step_index":10509,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-26T13:18:44Z","thinking":"The structure appears to be centered around plugins, each with a defined directory. Key components within these plugin directories are marker manifests, skill definitions, custom agent templates, and potentially rule sets. This hierarchical structure likely enables modularity and extensibility of the system.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"search_web","args":{"query":"\"\\\"Antigravity CLI\\\" \\\"plugins\\\" \\\"skills\\\" \\\"rules\\\" \\\"hooks\\\" \\\"sidecars\\\"\"","toolAction":"\"Searching for complete Antigravity CLI structure\"","toolSummary":"\"Search complete AGY structure\""}}]}
{"step_index":10510,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-26T13:18:49Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-26T13:18:49Z\nCompleted At: 2026-09-26T13:18:52Z\nThe search for \"\"Antigravity CLI\" \"plugins\" \"skills\" \"rules\" \"hooks\" \"sidecars\"\" returned the following summary:\nAntigravity CLI is a terminal-based interface for Google’s **Antigravity** agentic development platform. It provides a lightweight, keyboard-centric way to interact with AI agents for coding, refactoring, and project automation.\n\nThe platform uses a modular architecture where customizations can be bundled into **Plugins**. Key components of the Antigravity ecosystem include:\n\n### Core Customization Components\n*   **Plugins:** Namespaced bundles that act as a single deployable unit. They contain a required `plugin.json` manifest and can house skills, agents, rules, MCP (Model Context Protocol) servers, and hooks. When installed, the CLI stages these files (typically under `~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/plugins/`) for the agent to discover and load.\n*   **Skills:** Reusable agent capabilities defined in `SKILL.md` files. They allow agents to perform specific tasks or workflows (e.g., specific git management or testing patterns) and can be distributed within plugins.\n*   **Rules:** Markdown files that provide persistent, manually defined constraints to guide agent behavior, code style, and architectural patterns. Rules can be scoped to a directory or applied globally, with various activation modes such as \"always on\" or \"model decision.\"\n*   **Hooks:** Custom scripts or shell commands triggered at specific points during the agent's execution loop. They are used to enforce rules, execute linters, or capture diagnostics.\n*   **Sidecars:** Specialized, often automated, background processes or commands. Examples include scheduled tasks (Cron sidecars) that help orchestrate long-running or auxiliary workflows outside the main agent conversation.\n\n### Usage in the CLI\nThese components are managed and interacted with through the CLI, often using slash commands (e.g., `/agents` to monitor subagents). The CLI is designed for high-speed interaction, supporting:\n*   **Subagents:** Independent, concurrent agent sessions that allow the main agent to delegate tasks (like documentation lookup or build validation) in the background.\n*   **Terminal Sandbox:** A security mechanism that leverages native OS features (such as `nsjail`, `sandbox-exec`, or `AppContainer`) to isolate the agent's local shell commands and protect the host system.\n*   **Shared Harness:** The CLI shares the same core agent engine as Antigravity 2.0 and Antigravity IDE, ensuring that agent capabilities, settings, and customizations are consistent across all surfaces."}
{"step_index":10511,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-26T13:18:52Z","content":"«──────────────────────────────»\n*অফিসিয়াল আর্টিকেল ভিত্তিক AGY CLI স্ট্রাকচার*\n«──────────────────────────────»\n\nইরাক ভাইয়া,\n\nআপনি একদম নিখুঁত বিষয়টি ধরেছেন! পূর্বে আমি\nসিএলআই-এর ভেতরের ওএস রানটাইম ক্যাশ ও লগ\nফোল্ডার (`brain/`, `.system_generated/`, `db`)\nতুলে ধরেছিলাম।\n\nকিন্তু গুগল এন্টিগ্র্যাভিটির **অফিসিয়াল আর্টিকেল\nও স্ট্যান্ডার্ড স্পেসিফিকেশন** (`antigravity.google`)\nঅনুযায়ী, AGY CLI মূলত একটি **মডিউলার প্লাগইন,\nস্কিল ও সাইডকার কেন্দ্রিক আর্কিটেকচার**\n(Plugin-Centric Customization Architecture)।\n\nঅফিসিয়াল আর্টিকেল অনুযায়ী সঠিক কাঠামোটি নিচে\nতুলে ধরছি:\n\n«──────────────────────────────»\n*১. প্লাগইন ডিরেক্টরি স্ট্রাকচার (Plugins)*\n«──────────────────────────────»\nঅফিসিয়াল আর্টিকেলে প্লাগইন হলো এজেন্টের সমস্ত\nক্ষমতাকে একত্রিত করে প্যাকেজ করার স্ট্যান্ডার্ড একক:\n\n*লোকেশন:*\n`~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/plugins/<plugin_name>/`\n\n```\n<plugin_name>/\n├── plugin.json         (বাধ্যতামূলক ম্যানিফ\n<truncated 2607 bytes>\nত্তিক:\n`~/.gemini/config/plugins/<plugin>/sidecars/`\n\n```\nsidecars/\n└── <sidecar_name>/\n    ├── sidecar.json    (প্রসেস ও ট্রিগার কনফিগ)\n    └── script.py       (ব্যাকগ্রাউন্ড ডেমন স্ক্রিপ্ট)\n```\n\n«──────────────────────────────»\n*৪. সেটিংস ও স্যান্ডবক্স আর্কিটেকচার*\n«──────────────────────────────»\n* *কনফিগারেশন:*\n  `~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/settings.json`\n  (টার্মিনাল থেকে `/settings` বা `/config`\n  কমান্ডে নিয়ন্ত্রণযোগ্য)।\n* *টার্মিনাল স্যান্ডবক্স:*\n  হোস্ট সিস্টেম সুরক্ষিত রাখতে লিনাক্সের `nsjail`\n  দ্বারা বিচ্ছিন্ন ও সুরক্ষিত কমান্ড শেল।\n* *সাব-এজেন্ট হার্নেস:*\n  `/agents` কমান্ডের মাধ্যমে ব্যাকগ্রাউন্ডে\n  সমান্তরাল সাব-এজেন্ট মনিটরিং।\n\n«──────────────────────────────»\n*সারসংক্ষেপ*\n«──────────────────────────────»\nঅফিসিয়াল আর্টিকেল অনুযায়ী AGY CLI মূলত:\n১. `plugins/` (বান্ডিল প্যাকেজ),\n২. `.agents/skills/` (কাজের ক্ষমতা),\n৩. `rules/` (আচরণের সীমা), এবং\n৪. `sidecars/` (ব্যাকগ্রাউন্ড ডেমন্স)-এর\nএকটি সুসংগঠিত মডিউলার আর্কিটেকচার।","thinking":"Incorrectly provided a filesystem dump. The intended response should detail the official plugin architecture, not the underlying OS directories. The initial focus should have been on the publicly documented customization methods like plugins, skills, and rules, per the official Google Antigravity documentation.\n\n\nThe focus should be on the modular plugin architecture. This involves understanding the structure within the `plugins/` directory, including the required `plugin.json` manifest and subdirectories for skills, agents, rules, and configurations. Skill scopes define how these modular components are integrated within the broader system.\n\n\n","truncated_fields":["content"]}
