{"step_index":10518,"source":"MODEL","type":"GENERIC","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-26T13:24:12Z","content":"Created At: 2026-09-26T13:24:12Z\nCompleted At: 2026-09-26T13:24:14Z\nThe search for \"site:antigravity.google \"reset\" OR \"uninstall\" OR \"clean\" OR \"default\" \"agy\"\" returned the following summary:\nFor tasks related to resetting, uninstalling, or cleaning configurations in the Antigravity (AGY) CLI, refer to the following documented commands and procedures:\n\n### **Resetting and Cleaning**\n*   **Reset Keybindings:** To reset your keybindings to their default state, delete the `keybindings.json` file located at `~/.gemini/antigravity-cli/keybindings.json`[1].\n*   **Clear Conversation History:** Use the slash command `/clear` to clear the current prompt and start a new conversation session[1].\n*   **Delete Conversations:** To remove obsolete threads, highlight the conversation in the picker and press `Ctrl + Delete`[2].\n*   **Clear Screen:** Press `Ctrl + L` to clear the terminal output[1].\n\n### **Uninstalling**\n*   **Uninstall Plugins:** To remove a plugin and clean up its associated configuration registries, use the command[3]:\n    ```bash\n    agy plugin uninstall <plugin_name>\n    ```\n\n### **Execution Modes & Defaults**\n*   **Default Mode:** The CLI operates in `default` mode by default, which pauses for interactive diff reviews before applying changes[4]. You can cycle between `default`, `accept-edits`, and `plan` modes using `Shift + Tab` within the prompt box[4].\n*   **Settings:** Configurations are categorized into four scopes to keep settings \"clean and isolated\"[5]. By default, clicking **Settings** opens the configuration for the active project, or the global settings if no project is open[5].\n\nFor more advanced troubleshooting or configuration management, consult the [Antigravity CLI Documentation](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGQzjLmYqiVCjt6C4gTdScfqv9MfGfAvJdLW7CK7A-QS-FLN